      "date": "2026-07-07 06:12:35.000000000",
      "message": "Patch Set 1:\n\n(1 comment)\n\nExperimental feature testing in progress, please pay attention to the comments\n\nThe functional substitutions all check out: S_IRWXU/G/O -> 0700/0070/0007, S_IRWXUGO -> 0777, S_IXUGO -> 0111, S_IROTH/S_IWOTH/S_IXOTH -> 0004/0002/0001, and the split console strings re-concatenate to the same text, so nothing changes at runtime.\n\nOne readability concern noted inline. More broadly, checkpatch --fix-inplace turned several self-documenting symbolic mode masks into bare octal magic numbers; Lustre style generally prefers named constants over magic values, so if this is refreshed it may be worth leaving the symbolic forms in the ACL/permission bit-math where they read more clearly.",
      "accounts_in_message": [],
      "_revision_number": 1
    },
